  <revision rev="3" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>332792c30b6216c299cfaa018b37446e</srcmd5>
    <version>0.83.0</version>
    <time>1791575032</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>- Update to 0.83.0:
  * Deduplication now compares referenced models
  * Specialized dynamic-scope models shift generated class names
  * Dynamic ref resolution scope for inline resources and merged refs
  * Constraints are now emitted on recursive container fields
  * Stricter runtime validation of recursive container payloads
  * Protobuf weak imports can not longer escape the temporary directory
    (CVE-2026-107377, bsc#1284763)
  * Python union annotations preserve unsupported member types
  * Safe frozen set items use native Pydantic hash generation
  * Constrained root aliases retain their validation
  * Reject unsupported msgspec enum members
  * Aliases now abort generation on conflicts or invalid names
  * MCP tools schema-instance values preserved verbatim
  * allOf merge modes now intersect bounds and enums
  * Nested Avro bytes and fixed defaults are now decoded to bytes
  * Dictionary defaults now render as factories for pydantic v2 dataclasses
  * Avro duration defaults now decode to timedelta
  * XML Schema nillable now recognizes the 1 lexical value
  * Multiple enum sources in a union are converted
  * Combined XSD pattern facets change generated regexes
  * Parser source loading, run state, output-model capabilities, field-name
    policies, and input-model transport have been separated to clarify
    internal ownership
  * Root-model collapsing tracks references incrementally, and the built-in
    formatter skips unnecessary string normalization
  * x-enum-descriptions now accepts null entries, allowing schemas with
    missing individual enum descriptions to generate successfully
  * Pydantic v2 extra-property keys now enforce propertyNames
  * minProperties/maxProperties now generate runtime validators</comment>
    <requestid>1383624</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
